<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kilij Arslan II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1192">1192</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kilij Arslan II was sultan of the Seljuk <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultanate-of-rum">Sultanate of Rum</a> from 1156 to 1192. He annexed the lands of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danishmendids">Danishmendids</a> in the 1170s and destroyed a Byzantine army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuel-i-komnenos">Manuel I Komnenos</a> at Myriokephalon in 1176, ending Byzantine hopes of recovering central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>. In old age he divided his realm among his sons, which led to civil war.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kilij-arslan-ii.jpg" alt="Kilij Arslan II" width="320" height="409" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 1156-92 artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sultan_Kilij_Arslan_II_(portrait)_in_a_tile_from_Alaeddin_Palace,_Konya,_1156-92.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
